blurb: The Board of Education held its first FY26 budget workshop, where the superintendent
  presented a budget with significant staff reductions due to declining enrollment
  and rising taxpayer costs. Board members, staff, and the public voiced strong concerns
  over the proposed cuts to student-facing roles and curriculum leadership, setting
  the stage for difficult decisions ahead.
